 remains very much in the pipeline  the project was actually given the name  flashpoint back in 2017 which dc fans  will no doubt remember as an epic event  from the comics that saw the flash turn  the whole universe on its head to save  his mother the first official look at  the flash appeared to confirm that andy  muschetti's movie will follow the  classic arc pretty closely miller  introduced a sneak peek of the movie at  dc fandom 2021 in which the flash  appears to enter his childhood home and  reunite with his late mother fans will  no doubt have immediately recognized the  voice narrating the trailer as michael  keaton's batman who according to  muschetti plays a substantial role in  the film ben affleck will briefly  reprise his batman role too while sasha  kaye will debut as supergirl the flash  arrives on june 23 2023 but given ezra  miller's recent allegations chances are  this film might be delayed further  kevin feige gave away nothing about  captain marvel 2 when he revealed his  mcu phase 4 plans in 2019 but we now  know a whole lot more about the upcoming  sequel first off it's not called captain  marvel 2 at all instead the movie is  titled the marvels no doubt thanks to  its trio of headlining superheroes brie  larson will reprise the role of carol  danvers of course and she will be facing  off against zoe ashton who has been cast  as a thus far unidentified villain at  the same time an aged up version of  monica rambo will be featured monica had  previously appeared in the first captain  marvel movie as a young girl and in the  marvels tiana paris will play an older  version of the daughter of carol's late  best friend paris previously portrayed  monica in one division which laid the  groundwork for her transformation into  the superhero photon the marvels will  also star amon valani's kamala khan a  captain marvel super fan starring in the  disney plus series ms marvel the  coronavirus pandemic slowed the process  but production on the marvels reportedly  began in earnest in early january 2021  that same month brie larson spoke to  lily singh about the hiring of director  nia decosta who was set to become the  first black woman to direct a movie in  the mcu mia's amazing and she got the  job because she was the best person for  the job that's my that's one of my  favorite parts about this is she just  gave an incredible presentation  the marvels will land in theaters on  july 28 2023 check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite movies are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

